{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (config_004, acc=0.520) is our best RNA encoder, clearly outperforming pca_n2000 (config_001, acc=0.485). Image alone (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak, so the RNA modality is the primary driver. Uncertainty: We have no data on whether multiprofile aggregation adds value over singleprofile for the best encoder. This is a fundamental design axis that will determine the strategy for all downstream multimodal experiments. Question: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly extends our best singleprofile result by adding multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool), isolating whether multiple profiles carry complementary signal. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a minimal, clean change from our strongest configuration (only profile_setting and the required aggregation differ), it tests a design decision that propagates to every multimodal config, and using avgpool (rather than transformer) keeps the experiment simple so we can attribute any change to the multiprofile representation itself. If multiprofile helps, subsequent experiments should prioritize multiprofile multimodal configs; if not, we can focus budget on singleprofile multimodal or better image encoders."
}

